Z||000004||Archie||11-29-2001||12:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Denny:<BR><B>I've been away for 5 days, and get home and find no messages from Archie's Technet. Is the server down?<P>And no, my mailbox did not fill up.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It will be working now.<P>That server is strange, if it gets even one bounced message, it will shut you off. When someone askd me to check out their account for a problem all it tells me is if you are "on" or "off" the only thing it tells me is that you had a "soft Bounce" whatever that means. It doesn't tell me when, where or why.<P>Anyway, I turned it back on.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000005||Denny||11-29-2001||08:13 AM||||Thanks Archie!||||reg||6
Z||000006||Denny||11-29-2001||09:12 AM||||Hey Archie!<P>I see my test message made it to the list ( <A HREF="http://www.topica.com/lists/fiero-technet/read?" TARGET=_blank>http://www.topica.com/lists/fiero-technet/read?</A> ), but I'm still not receiving email from it.<P>?????????????||||reg||9
Z||000007||FieroLT1||11-29-2001||09:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B> the only thing it tells me is that you had a "soft Bounce" whatever that means. It doesn't tell me when, where or why.<BR>Anyway, I turned it back on.<BR>Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hi Archie,<P>  (Computer Engineer Hat ON) A "soft bounce" occurs when a valid MX record was found for the email address the list server is trying to send to. All that means is that the person behind the address does in fact exists. Versus a "Hard" or Forced bounce, which you'd get when it happens to be a bougus address or the case of a disabled mail account. Soft bounces should be set on the list server configuration as to be retried for up to five days or so, as these errors often mean the mail server on the receiving end is temporarily offline in which case the person will eventually get their email without being kicked out.<P><BR>Hope this helps,<BR><P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
